@startuml contract-lifecycle
'==============================================================================
' Figure (Chapter II): State machine of the Contract aggregate.
' States from the Contract.Status value object (draft, active, expiring,
' terminated, archived; expired implied by the archive rule). Transitions
' are labelled with the command or event that triggers them.
' Render:  plantuml -tpdf contract-lifecycle.puml      (or -tpng)
'==============================================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
hide empty description

[*]        --> Draft       : RegisterContract
Draft      --> Active      : approval finalised
Active     --> Expiring    : notice window opens
Expiring   --> Active      : UpdateContract (renewal)
Active     --> Terminated  : TerminateContract
Expiring   --> Expired     : end date passed
Terminated --> Archived    : ArchiveContract
Expired    --> Archived    : ArchiveContract
Archived   --> [*]

note as N
  Soft delete (tombstone) and restore are available
  from any state and are omitted here for clarity.
end note
@enduml
